    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0852" n="1642" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v01p2/pg1642"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">398.18 ICEM/10–654</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Intergovernmental Committee on
                        European Migration (Gibson) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-10-06">6th October, 1954</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to submit enclosed a
                    memorandum on the U.S. Appropriations rider attached to Public Law 665<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d265-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg844">p. 844</ref>, the
                    provisions of which make the payments of U.S. contributions to the Migration
                    Committee in 1955 conditional on security clearance of migrants to countries of
                    the Western Hemisphere being based on “reasonable standards”.</p>
                <p>In the memorandum I have endeavoured to make some suggestions on general lines
                    for the implementation of the rider which I trust you may consider of some
                    value.</p>
                <p>However, after careful study of the subject in the light of the interpretation by
                    the U.S. Congress of the intent and text of the rider, of the tentative plan of
                    its implementation, suggested to me by Mr. George Warren on September 17th, on
                    behalf of the Department of State and of my obligations as Director of the
                    Intergovernmental Committee for European Migration, I find that, before taking
                    further action, I have to ask you for an official interpretation of the rider
                    and for a ruling which would enlighten me on the conditions which the Committee
                    should fulfil in order to qualify for the payments under its provisions.</p>
                <p>I have the honour to be, Sir,</p>
                <p>Your obedient Servant</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh Gibson</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d265-a1.xml" xpointer="d265-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d265-a2.xml" xpointer="d265-a2"/>
